[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"350","stub":{"id":"350","section":"Rte. 56 to Nash","altname":"","river":"Tye, South Fork","difficulty":"V","states":["USA-VRG"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"48","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"takeout","description":"The take-out for this section is the confluence of the South Fork Tye and the North Fork Tye, near Nash, VA. A new landowner has strung bard-wire fence all the way to the state bridge here, making access difficult recently. Most folks park nearby a short walk up the North Fork Tye at the church on North Fork Rd.","id":"113879","location":{"latitude":"37.856499","longitude":"-79.046097"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"put-in","description":"The put-in map being auto-generated by this website may not be correct. For this section of the South Fork Tye the put-in is the Rt. 56 bridge that is around 3.7 miles upstream of the confluence at Nash, VA. The put-in is a state highway bridge but respect nearby private property.","id":"108643","location":{"latitude":"37.852993","longitude":"-79.103451"},"name":"Put In","distance":"2.09","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"100735915","title":null,"post_date":"2009-02-17 05:00:00+00","detail":"The put-in access point that we used for years on Rt. 56 is now heavily posted. The guy who lives immediately below the bridge has not been open to kayakers on the creek. I don't know what to tell you about getting on to the creek other than this: you can do the lower half of the creek by putting on at the USFS Crabtree Falls parking lot. You will not get to paddle Fodderstep and a few other good rapids this way though.","user":{"name":"Gordon Dalton"}}],"photos":[{"id":"1081","ext":"mov","post_id":"3801","description":"The S. Fork lacks big distinctive drops like its sister, the N. Fork*.\r\nIt does boast consistent gradient and massive boulder gardens.\r\nLot's of texture to keep a paddler very busy for the duration\r\nof the trip.\r\n\r\n\r\n*The glaring exception to this generalization is Fodder Step,\r\nwhich is possibly the most exceptional rapid on either stream.\r\n\r\nQuicktime movie: Download free player at http://www.apple.com/quicktime/download/","caption":"Creek action, SFT","poi_name":"fodder step, double boof, more...","subject":"Hugh Robinson, Gordon Dalton, Glen Piegari","author":"Glen Piegari","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1081","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1081"}},{"id":"4722","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4142","description":"","caption":"Rapid Sequence One","poi_name":"","subject":"Hill Harman","author":"David Hoffman","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/4722","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/4722"}},{"id":"10616","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3116","description":"This is fairly typical South Tye boogie-water. Taken in the late '90's so I forget which part of the creek.","caption":"Typical South Tye","poi_name":"","subject":"Sweet Daddy","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/10616","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/10616"}},{"id":"12822","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"8684","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/12822","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/12822"}},{"id":"1089","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3115","description":"","caption":"Limbo-Log, SFT","poi_name":"Limbo-Log (right line)","subject":"Gordon Dalton","author":"Lauren Collingwood","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1089","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1089"}},{"id":"18258","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3117","description":"","caption":"Fodderstep","poi_name":"Fodderstep","subject":"Alex Clayden","author":"Sid Crocker","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/18258","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/18258"}},{"id":"18259","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3118","description":"","caption":"Fodderstep, from upstream","poi_name":"Fodderstep","subject":"Sid Crocker","author":"Alex Clayden?","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/18259","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/18259"}},{"id":"3133","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3119","description":"","caption":"Fodderstep","poi_name":"Fodderstep","subject":"Harris Haynie","author":"Gordon Dalton","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3133","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3133"}},{"id":"1057","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3802","description":"","caption":"Jeff's Jolly, SFT","poi_name":"Jeff's Jolly","subject":"Gordon Dalton","author":"Glen Piegari","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1057","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1057"}},{"id":"4723","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4142","description":"","caption":"Rapid Sequence Two","poi_name":"","subject":"Hill Harman","author":"David Hoffman","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/4723","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/4723"}},{"id":"4724","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4142","description":"","caption":"Sequence Shot Three","poi_name":"","subject":"Hill Harman","author":"David Hoffman","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/4724","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/4724"}},{"id":"4892","ext":"mpg","post_id":"4142","description":"","caption":"SFT Rapid","poi_name":"","subject":"Dave Hoffman","author":"Hill Harman","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/4892","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/4892"}},{"id":"4891","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4142","description":"Dave smashed the crap out of his hand on this run.  It was a little bony at this level (which I don't know).","caption":"Doing the limbo","poi_name":"Limbo Log","subject":"Dave Hoffman","author":"Hill Harman","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/4891","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/4891"}}],"detail":{"id":"350","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"Thanks to Mike M., here is the footage of an early run on the South Fork Tye:\n\n[www.youtube.com/watch](http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c9RrE29VqJ0)   ( http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c9RrE29VqJ0 )\n\nGreg Gil (in the blue Corsica) was also along for our first descent of the North Fork and he shot video of that. If anyone knows where he has gone please let me know and i'll try to get that footy as well. Thanks, Gordon Dalton\n\n\\*\\*\\*The map being auto-generated by the AW Website is not accuate. It shows _both_ sections of the South Fork. Note that the put-in is not accurate for this section of the SFT.\\*\\*\\*\n\nThe South Fork Tye is the sister run to its nextdoor neighbor, the famous North Fork Tye. They make a great combination of runs to hit in the same day. Or set an even loftier goal of getting a 'Full Nelson' - runs on four of this area's short class V runs. (Forks of the Piney, Statons Creek, South Rockfish, and several other fun class V runs are within a half-hour radius).\n\nThe South Fork Tye (SFT) is not quite as 'defined' as the North Fork, but its signature rapid - Fodderstep - is arguably biggest drop of these two streams. Although it doesn't have as many 'big' drops as the NFT, the South Fork is actually slightly steeper; probably because it is even more continuous. It never lets up. The stream could be described as continuous class IV+ to V- boulder gardens, with a constant threat of strainers or fallen logs.\n\nIf you are looking for easier parking/access, or just a shorter option, consider putting-in at the Crabtree Falls Parking Area. (37.85106, -79.07898) This is a National Park fee area but provides easy access to a little more than half of the run. There is also a working pay phone near the creek in the lower parking area here. This lower section includes Limblog, Jeff's Jolly, and Fleckenstein's, but does not include Fodderstep.","averageGradient":"219","maxGradient":null,"length":"5.9","correlations":[{"reachID":"350","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"900","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"7000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"TYE RIVER NEAR LOVINGSTON, VA","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"02027000","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"48","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"2.91","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"